    <string name="setup_title">Shizuku setup</string>
    <string name="setup_status_title">Current status</string>
    <string name="setup_steps_title">Setup steps</string>
    <string name="setup_step_number">Step %1$d</string>
    <string name="setup_step_1_title">Install the Shizuku app</string>
    <string name="setup_step_1_desc">Install the official Shizuku app (package moe.shizuku.privileged.api). DexBoost cannot work without it.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_2_title">Enable Developer options and a debugging connection</string>
    <string name="setup_step_2_desc">On Android 11 and later, turn on Developer options, then Wireless debugging. Alternatively, connect the phone to a computer and authorise ADB over USB.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_3_title">Start Shizuku and pair it</string>
    <string name="setup_step_3_desc">Open the Shizuku app and tap Start. For wireless debugging, use the pairing flow Shizuku shows and confirm when asked. Wait until Shizuku reports that it is running.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_4_title">Grant DexBoost permission when prompted</string>
    <string name="setup_step_4_desc">Back in DexBoost, request Shizuku permission and tap Allow in the Shizuku dialog. Until you allow it, DexBoost cannot run any privileged command.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_5_title">After a reboot, start Shizuku again</string>
    <string name="setup_step_5_desc">The Shizuku server does not survive a reboot. Repeat the wireless-debugging activation and start Shizuku again before DexBoost can work.</string>
    <string name="setup_troubleshooting_title">Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="setup_trouble_1_title">Shizuku is not running</string>
    <string name="setup_trouble_1_desc">Open the Shizuku app and check whether it reports running. If not, make sure wireless debugging or ADB is enabled, then tap Start in Shizuku and complete pairing.</string>
    <string name="setup_trouble_2_title">Permission denied</string>
    <string name="setup_trouble_2_desc">Request permission again from DexBoost and tap Allow. If you previously tapped Deny, open the Shizuku app, find DexBoost in its authorised apps list, and allow it there.</string>
    <string name="setup_trouble_3_title">Binder died (connection lost while using DexBoost)</string>
    <string name="setup_trouble_3_desc">The connection to the Shizuku server was lost. Open the Shizuku app, confirm it is running again, allow DexBoost if asked, then retry. If it keeps happening, restart Shizuku from its Start screen.</string>
    <string name="setup_trouble_4_title">Shizuku app not found</string>
    <string name="setup_trouble_4_desc">Check that the installed app is the official Shizuku app with package moe.shizuku.privileged.api. If it is not installed, install it, then follow the setup steps.</string>
